<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27941" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mantŭa</span></b> , ae,
		f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				city of</i> Gallia Transpadana, <i>on the Mincius,
				in whose vicinity was Andes, the birthplace of Virgil</i>,
			still called <i>Mantua</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 19,
				23, § 130</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 24,
				10, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 10, 200</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mantua Vergilio gaudet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 3, 15, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sil. 8, 595</span></i>.— Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mantŭānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Mantua</i> or <i>to
				Virgil, Mantuan, Virgilian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fama,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 4, 7, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Maro,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Min. Fel. Octav. 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vates,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 2, § 212</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">also called Mantuanus Homerus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 16</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">and Mantuanus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 5, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carmina,</span>”
				<i>Virgil's poems</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 46</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
